# What must not go into the image.
#
# The build stage does COPY . ., so anything not excluded here is baked into a
# layer — and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, whatever the
# final stage does afterwards.

# Previous runs. These hold evidence, redacted credential reports and sandbox
# homes from real runs against real clouds. Nothing about them belongs in a
# published image, and they are the largest thing in the tree.
artifacts/
bin/

# History, including every secret ever committed and reverted.
.git/
.github/

# Local configuration that would otherwise override what a user mounts.
.env
*.local.yaml
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# Noise: nothing here affects the build.
*.log
*.md
docs/
examples/
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
